A MESSAGE FROM TELEPORT

 
 From Zero Trust to Agent Trust 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 AI agents are neither human nor machine — they act at machine speed with human unpredictability, and can produce globally destructive outcomes.


 Zero Trust was built for a different threat model. Agent Trust extends it for the one you're actually facing.


 Read the white paper. 


 
 &nbsp; 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 4. + This 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Duolingo stepped in to restore the 301-day streak of a 10-year-old who had an unexpected trip to the hospital. But now lots more people are sending in their excuses.

 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 &nbsp; 
A MESSAGE FROM TELEPORT

 
 Collective agent activity can be destructive 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Agents can individually stay fully in-scope yet still converge on the same fix, saturate I/O and crash a cluster.


 No single agent exceeded its permissions. No audit log flagged anything suspicious. Zero Trust has no language for this swarm-level failure.


 Agent Trust bridges the gap. 


 
